## Source
Path B UX dry-run (0152), severity: **Low**

## Context
The README Quick start section shows `validate`, `check`, and `ready` — but not
`erg new`, the command to create a ticket. A user skimming the README to evaluate
the tool never sees how to create a ticket. They must run `erg --help --all` to
discover it (which is documented, but is a secondary path).

## Fix
Add one example to Quick start:

```bash
tickets/erg new "My first task"
# → CREATED 0001-my-first-task.erg
```

## Exit criteria
- [ ] README Quick start includes at least one `erg new` example with expected output
